{"id": 17, "ts": 1781184139.587314, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I appreciate Sarah\u2019s confidence in Candidate\u202fC\u2019s reliability and crew atmosphere, and I recognize James\u2019s emphasis on Candidate\u202fB\u2019s strong stress resilience and technical aptitude. However, the long\u2011distance pilot role demands not only operational reliability but also a willingness to continuously develop skills for evolving international routes. Candidate\u202fC, while reliable and quick in decision\u2011making, is noted as \u201cnot very willing to further his education,\u201d which raises concerns about his adaptability and long\u2011term growth. In contrast, Candidate\u202fB demonstrates very strong stress handling, excellent weather\u2011assessment ability, and solid technical competence, and his conscientiousness suggests a solid foundation for reliability. Although B\u2019s pretentiousness and occasional tone issues are serious, they are interpersonal behaviors that can be addressed through targeted crew\u2011resource\u2011management training and coaching, whereas a lack of educational drive is harder to remediate.\nGiven the current evidence, I would provisionally recommend **Candidate\u202fB** as the best overall fit, while we continue to seek any additional insight on Candidate\u202fD\u2019s crew\u2011cooperation and communication, which remain unknown."}
